/P 102 0 R
/T (Traditional coding refers to the conventional practice of writing software using programming languages, where developers manually author every instruction that the computer will execute. This approach demands a thorough understanding of programming syntax, data structures, algorithms, software architecture, and design patterns. Traditional coding provides developers with complete control over how an application behaves, how it is structured, and how it integrates with other systems.)
/E (Traditional coding refers to the conventional practice of writing software using programming languages, where developers manually author every instruction that the computer will execute. This approach demands a thorough understanding of programming syntax, data structures, algorithms, software architecture, and design patterns. Traditional coding provides developers with complete control over how an application behaves, how it is structured, and how it integrates with other systems.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [11]
