153 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 103 0 R
/T (Traditional coding has existed since the earliest days of computing, evolving from assembly languages to high-level languages such as COBOL, C, and eventually modern languages like Python and JavaScript. Low-code, by contrast, emerged as a response to the growing demand for software that outpaced the supply of skilled developers. Early precursors included fourth-generation languages \(4GLs\) and rapid application development \(RAD\) tools in the 1990s. The modern low-code movement gained momentum in the 2010s as cloud computing matured and businesses sought to accelerate digital transformation without expanding their engineering teams proportionally.)
/E (Traditional coding has existed since the earliest days of computing, evolving from assembly languages to high-level languages such as COBOL, C, and eventually modern languages like Python and JavaScript. Low-code, by contrast, emerged as a response to the growing demand for software that outpaced the supply of skilled developers. Early precursors included fourth-generation languages \(4GLs\) and rapid application development \(RAD\) tools in the 1990s. The modern low-code movement gained momentum in the 2010s as cloud computing matured and businesses sought to accelerate digital transformation without expanding their engineering teams proportionally.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
