167 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 104 0 R
/T (With low-code platforms, security responsibilities are shared between the platform vendor and the organization. Vendors typically handle infrastructure security, patching, and compliance certifications, which can reduce the burden on internal teams. However, this also means that organizations have less direct control over the security posture of their applications and must trust the vendor's practices. This matters for a loan application system, which holds personal and financial details of applicants.)
/E (With low-code platforms, security responsibilities are shared between the platform vendor and the organization. Vendors typically handle infrastructure security, patching, and compliance certifications, which can reduce the burden on internal teams. However, this also means that organizations have less direct control over the security posture of their applications and must trust the vendor's practices. This matters for a loan application system, which holds personal and financial details of applicants.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
168 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 104 0 R
/T (Traditional coding places full responsibility for security in the hands of the development team, requiring expertise in secure coding practices, vulnerability testing, and ongoing patch management. This offers complete control but also demands a higher level of security expertise within the team.)
/E (Traditional coding places full responsibility for security in the hands of the development team, requiring expertise in secure coding practices, vulnerability testing, and ongoing patch management. This offers complete control but also demands a higher level of security expertise within the team.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [7]
